/* R12 — LN PO_Update contract. Identical to PoAccept.request.jsonata bar the POStatus literal; see that
   file for the full rationale on D6 / D7 / D8 / D24 and the "[object Object]" hazard.

   The document root here is the NEGOTIATION (portalEntity PoNegotiation, entityId = the negotiation id), but
   poNegotiation-v2 exposes `lines` in exactly the same shape as the PO document, so this text is
   interchangeable with the other two. The per-line dates are already the AGREED ones: the builder overlays
   each approved negotiation line's negotiatedDeliveryDate onto the PO's own line set (D10), because
   ApprovePoNegotiationCommand deliberately does not mutate PurchaseOrderLine.

   The untouched negotiation detail (original vs negotiated qty / price) stays available under
   `negotiationLines` if LN ever wants it — nothing maps it today.

   !! POStatus "Negotiated" is a WIRE-ONLY literal. PoStatus has no such member: approving a negotiation sets
   the PO to Approved and the negotiation to Approved. Never copy this string into an eligibility gate — a
   gate is strict-true/fail-closed, so `poStatus = "Negotiated"` would skip every negotiation silently. */
{
    "PurchaseOrderDetail": {
        "CompanyCode": companyCode,
        "OrderNo": poNumber,
        "PlannedDeliveryDate": headerDeliveryDate != null ? headerDeliveryDate,
        "ConfirmedReceiptDate": headerDeliveryDate != null ? headerDeliveryDate,
        "POStatus": "Negotiated",
        "Lines": [lines[deliveryDate != null].{
            "LineNo": $string(positionNo),
            "SeqNo": $string(sequenceNo),
            "PlannedDeliveryDate": deliveryDate
        }]
    }
}
